On Fri, 2006-01-27 at 11:04 -0600, Joy Latten wrote:
> I am converting the selinux testsuite policy to reference policy.
> The old test policy used the macros, can_setcon, can_setexec,
> can_setfscreate. These macros are not existent in the source for 
> current refpolicy. Will these macros be included in refpolicy or
> obsolete, or do I write them myself in the test module, or do they map
> to something else now? Just wondering what is the correct thing to do?

Some macros have been carried over from the example policy, but these
particular ones have not.  The equivalents for these in refpolicy are:

can_setcon(foo_t):

allow foo_t self:process setcurrent;
domain_dyntrans_type(foo_t)
selinux_get_fs_mount(foo_t)


can_setexec(foo_t):

allow foo_t self:process setexec;
selinux_get_fs_mount(foo_t)


can_setfscreate(foo_t):

allow foo_t self:process setfscreate;
selinux_get_fs_mount(foo_t)


I have also attached a copy of my notes (caveat: they are rough, and
there is no guarantee that it is all correct) on how old macros map up
to reference policy rules and interface calls.

